  "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{5}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{5}^{y}}{x}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{1}{x}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}{5}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{1}{x}{[\\frac{{5}^{y}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20615}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{1}{x}(\\frac{{5}^{1}-{5}^{0}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20615})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{1}{x}(\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20615})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20615}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20615}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20615}[\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x]_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20615}(\\operatorname{ln}\u20615-\\operatorname{ln}\u20611) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
